---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Conversations" description="How Woodhouse treats private conversations, public project facts and edited dispatches." path="/conversations/" image="/og/factory.jpg">
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <div class="page-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">WOODHOUSE</a><span>/</span><span>Conversations</span></nav>
        <p class="eyebrow">Editorial policy</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">Private by default. Published after review.</h1>
      </div>
      <aside class="page-intro__aside"><strong>An edited publication, not a transcript</strong>Woodhouse shares reviewed project facts and essays. Private working conversations stay private.</aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--reading">
      <article class="prose">
        <p>Woodhouse is a public record of reviewed work. Its project summaries describe an explicitly dated report; its dispatches explain lessons in their own words.</p>
        <h2>What appears here</h2>
        <p>Public project summaries, architecture, operating principles and edited engineering articles. Every project status carries a review date and a boundary describing what the source does not prove.</p>
        <h2>What stays private</h2>
        <p>Working conversation transcripts, private repository text, credentials and personal information. A useful idea from a private discussion can inform an article, but the discussion itself is not published by default.</p>
        <h2>How a source becomes a post</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>A human chooses the subject and the facts suitable for public use.</li>
          <li>Claims are checked against the selected source; missing or uncertain evidence stays visible.</li>
          <li>The edited result is reviewed before publication, with the source date and limits kept in view.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="callout">
          <p class="callout__title">Publication boundary</p>
          <p>This site has no public chat stream or automatic conversation publishing endpoint. Project and factory records remain reviewed snapshots.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/dispatches/">Read the edited dispatches <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
